  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of distinct <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> for which,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />As <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous and decreasing<br /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>-1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br />By intermediate value theorem (IVT),<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>possesses exactly one solution in [0, 1]. As <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn>&#160;</mrow></math>"
  }
